    "title": "What channel is North Carolina vs VCU on today? Time, TV schedule for March Madness game",
    "text": "March 19, 2026, 5:06 a.m. ETGREENVILLE, S.C. — The North Carolina Tar Heels play the VCU Rams in the opening round of the men’s 2026 NCAA Tournament.The sixth-seeded Tar Heels (24-8) and 11th-seeded Rams (27-7) tip off on Thursday, March 19 (6:50 p.m. ET, TNT) at Bon Secours Wellness Arena in Greenville, S.C. as part of the South Region. The winner will play No. 3 seed Illinois (24-8) or No. 14 Penn (18-11) on Saturday, March 21, for a spot in the Sweet 16 in Houston. Watch UNC vs VCU on Sling TVUNC and VCU are playing for the first time. The Tar Heels are making their 55th March Madness appearance, second only to Kentucky (63), and the Rams are in the tournament for the 21st time. Here's how to watch the UNC vs. VCU game today in the NCAA Tournament, including time, TV schedule and streaming information:What channel is UNC vs VCU on today in March Madness?TV channel: TNTStream: NCAA March Madness Live app | Sling TVUNC will tip off vs. VCU on TNT. Streaming options include the NCAA March Madness Live app and Sling TV. Announcers for the game are Ian Eagle, Bill Raftery, Grant Hill and Tracy Wolfson. Noah Eagle and LaPhonso Ellis will call the action for Westwood One radio.Watch UNC vs VCU on Sling TVJones Angell will have the radio call on the Tar Heel Sports Radio Network. Tyler Hansbrough and Tyler Zeller will rotate as game analysts, with Dave Nathan and Adam Lucas joining the broadcast for pregame, halftime and postgame. For local radio in Chapel Hill, the game can be found on 97.9 FM. Fans can listen for free online through the 97.9 FM Chapelboro website.UNC vs VCU start time in NCAA bracket Date: Thursday, March 19Time: 6:50 p.m. ETBuy UNC NCAA Tournament ticketsUNC and VCU will play at 6:50 p.m. ET at Bon Secours Wellness Arena in Greenville, S.C. UNC vs VCU odds in March MadnessOdds courtesy of BetMGM as of Tuesday, March 17. Odds will be posted as soon as they become available.Spread: UNC by 2 ½ pointsOver/under: 153 ½ pointsMoneyline: UNC (-150), VCU (+125)UNC basketball schedule 2025-26Below are the past five games of UNC's 2025-26 basketball season. For the full schedule, click here.Feb. 23: vs. Louisville (W, 77-74)Feb. 28: vs. Virginia Tech (W, 89-82)March 3: vs. Clemson (W, 67-63)March 7: at Duke (L, 76-61)March 12: vs. Clemson (L, 80-79) in ACC Tournament quarterfinalsMarch 19: vs. VCU in NCAA Tournament first round VCU basketball schedule 2025-26Below are the past five games of VCU's 2025-26 basketball season. For the full schedule, click here.March 3: vs. George Mason (W, 70-65)March 6: at Dayton (W, 68-62)March 13: vs. Duquesne (W, 71-66) in Atlantic 10 Conference Tournament quarterfinalsMarch 14: vs. Saint Joseph’s (W, 77-64) in Atlantic 10 Conference Tournament semifinalsMarch 15: vs. Dayton (W, 70-62) in Atlantic 10 Conference Tournament championshipMarch 19: vs. VCU in NCAA Tournament first roundRodd Baxley covers North Carolina Tar Heels athletics for The Fayetteville Observer as part of the USA TODAY Network. Follow his ACC coverage on X/Twitter or Bluesky: @RoddBaxley. Got questions regarding UNC? Send them torbaxley@usatodayco.com.",
